"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"GBW >= 20 MHz with CL = 2 pF requires gm1 >= 251 uS. Total power <= 400 uW implies total current <= 121 uA, so Itail <= 60 uA. Setting Itail = 50 uA (power = 330 uW, SR = 25 V/us). With I1 = 25 uA, to achieve gm1 ~ 300 uS, set W1/L1 = 20/0.5. For DC gain >= 40 dB (gm*ro >= 100), choose L ~ 0.5 - 0.7 um. To keep the mirror pole well above GBW (for PM >= 60 deg), keep W3/L3 compact: W3/L3 = 10/0.5 um gives gm3 ~ 180 uS and low mirror capacitance Cx. M5 sized at 15/0.7 um to maintain saturation with low Vdsat (~0.2 V) and high output impedance.\",\n  \"W1_um\": 20.0,\n  \"L1_um\": 0.5,\n  \"W3_um\": 10.0,\n  \"L3_um\": 0.5,\n  \"W5_um\": 15.0,\n  \"L5_um\": 0.7,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 50.0\n}"